  "id": "DrugBank_DB00942 - MONDO_17636",
  "verbalization": "Cycrimine is associated with Hemiparkinsonism-hemiatrophy Syndrome through a chain of indications involving Safinamide. The evidence suggests that Cycrimine may be repurposed for conditions such as Atypical Juvenile Parkinsonism, Hereditary Late Onset Parkinson Disease, and Early-onset Parkinsonism-intellectual Disability Syndrome, all of which are linked to Safinamide. Safinamide, in turn, is indicated for Hemiparkinsonism-hemiatrophy Syndrome, implying a potential therapeutic relationship between Cycrimine and this condition. The shared use of Safinamide in these indications suggests a possible mechanistic link, though the exact pathway remains unclear. The evidence supports a repurposing hypothesis, but further research is needed to clarify the specific mechanisms and clinical relevance.",
